<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Carib War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1772">1772</a>–<a href="/years/1773">1773</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Carib War was fought on Saint Vincent between British forces and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garifuna">Garifuna</a>, or Black Caribs, who resisted British surveyors dividing their land into plantations after the island was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1763. Unable to defeat them in the mountainous north, the British signed a treaty in 1773 that left the Garifuna a reserved territory under British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-carib-war.jpg" alt="First Carib War" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agostino Brunias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_William_Young_Conducting_a_Treaty_with_the_Black_Caribs_on_the_Island_of_St_Vincent,_1773.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
